' racing_quotes.bas -- the QuoteBank data and Quote$/FillIn$ that pick and
' fill a random line from it, split out of racing.bas so racing.bas's own
' code has room to grow: the full quote bank on top of the game no longer
' fit in the board's 128K program space. Loaded by racing.bas's very first
' statement (LIBRARY LOAD "B:/Games/racing_quotes.bas", RAM), which puts
' this in its own 128K PSRAM library slot -- separate from racing.bas's
' program space, and separate from the board's flash-saved library (the
' club's fonts), which this never touches and which is unaffected once
' the game exits. Build with: python mmbasic/build.py

Dim string qN$, qC$, qD$, qM$, qT$, qX$, qE$, qP$
Dim integer qLast(40)
' qSaid: one bit per line, set once that line's been said -- Quote$'s
' shuffle bag, so nobody hears the same mechanic/driver line twice until
' every line in that moment's bank has come up (then it reshuffles).
' 64 bits/category, so QuoteBank categories must stay at 64 lines or under
Dim integer qSaid(40)

' --- what they say: a bank of lines for each moment; Quote$ works through
' every line in a category before any of them repeat (see qSaid), so a
' long session doesn't start echoing itself. %N the player, %C the car,
' %D damage, %M money, %T lap time, %X target, %E what broke, %P a podium
' place ("1st"/"2nd"/"3rd"). Add lines freely: change a category's count
' to match, and keep it at 64 lines or under (qSaid's bitmask).
